---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Storyselling" description="The methodology for creating solution stories that unite clients and colleagues">
  <article class="rabbit-hole">
    <section class="hero-rabbit">
      <a href="/rabbit-holes/" class="back-link">← Rabbit Holes</a>
      <div class="rabbit-tenets">
        <span class="tenet">Story</span>
        <span class="tenet">Clarity</span>
      </div>
      <h1>Storyselling</h1>
      <p class="rabbit-tagline">Creating solution stories that unite clients and colleagues around your biggest problem</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">The Core Insight</h2>
      <div class="insight-box">
        <blockquote>
          "Every client needs a solution. So why do businesses keep selling just products?"
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          Most businesses fear solutions — they think it shrinks their audience. But the opposite is true: 
          <strong>solutions grow your market</strong>. Clients want frictionless success.
          Help them, and they'll help you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">The 5-Phase System</h2>
      <div class="methodology-grid">
        <div class="phase-card">
          <span class="phase-number">1</span>
          <h3>Big Problem</h3>
          <p>Research to identify the most profitable problem you're uniquely positioned to solve.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Solution Stack framework</li>
            <li>SWOT (as-is → to-be)</li>
            <li>5 client deep dives</li>
            <li>10 colleague interviews</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        
        <div class="phase-card">
          <span class="phase-number">2</span>
          <h3>Write Your Story</h3>
          <p>Transform research into compelling narratives across multiple formats.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>TED-style talk</li>
            <li>30-second explainer</li>
            <li>Movie poster</li>
            <li>One Newsletter</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        
        <div class="phase-card">
          <span class="phase-number">3</span>
          <h3>Testing Time</h3>
          <p>Validate with stakeholders before full rollout.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Stakeholder reveal</li>
            <li>Feedback loops</li>
            <li>Story refinement</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        
        <div class="phase-card">
          <span class="phase-number">4</span>
          <h3>Selling Your Story</h3>
          <p>Deploy unified messaging for internal and external audiences.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Single community narrative</li>
            <li>Client + colleague unity</li>
            <li>Cross-platform activation</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        
        <div class="phase-card">
          <span class="phase-number">5</span>
          <h3>Repairs & Upgrades</h3>
          <p>Continuous evolution to match changing needs.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Scheduled review cycles</li>
            <li>Metric monitoring</li>
            <li>Story iteration</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">The Revolutionary Concept</h2>
      <div class="concept-box">
        <h3>The Client-Colleague Cycle</h3>
        <p>
          Traditional businesses treat customers and colleagues as separate. 
          <strong>Storyselling treats them as one community</strong> — both invested in your success.
        </p>
        <div class="cycle-visual">
          <span>Clients → Insights →</span>
          <span>Colleagues → Better Products →</span>
          <span>Clients (repeat)</span>
        </div>
        <p class="key-quote">
          "Customers can become your best colleagues. Colleagues can become your best customers."
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">The Solution Stack</h2>
      <div class="stack-container">
        <p>A simpler alternative to the Business Model Canvas — four blocks that force clarity:</p>
        <div class="stack-grid">
          <div class="stack-item">
            <h4>Big Problem</h4>
            <p>What's the biggest problem you solve? Why does it exist? What's the cost?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stack-item">
            <h4>Solution</h4>
            <p>What are the components? How do you deliver it? One sentence that sums it up.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stack-item">
            <h4>Client</h4>
            <p>Market size. Your share. The parent market. How you grow.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stack-item">
            <h4>Our Business</h4>
            <p>Why you're the best provider. Your unique value. Success metrics.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section endorsement-section">
      <div class="endorsement-box">
        <blockquote>
          "He finds the essence of a brand and makes it simple to understand."
        </blockquote>
        <cite>— <strong>Ben Gross</strong>, Director, Electric Circus Digital</cite>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">Storyselling in Action</h2>
      <div class="example-box">
        <h3>Microsoft .NET — The Ballmer Case</h3>
        <p>
          In 2002, Microsoft needed developers to adopt .NET over Java. Steve Ballmer spent 
          <strong>34 years cultivating the developer community</strong>: creating MSDN, launching the MVP program, 
          hosting conferences, and ensuring engineers felt like heroes of Microsoft's story.
        </p>
        <p>
          His "Developers, developers, developers" speech wasn't just enthusiasm — it was the culmination of 
          decades of Storyselling. The result: .NET adoption that fuels Microsoft's success to this day.
        </p>
        <p class="outcome">Use Stack Overflow, Xbox Live, or Duolingo? You're benefiting from Ballmer's Storyselling.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">For Clients</h2>
      <div class="client-applications">
        <div class="application-card">
          <span class="persona-tag">Founder CEOs</span>
          <h4>"We're growing but lack clarity"</h4>
          <p>Start with the <strong>Solution Stack</strong> — distil your business to four blocks in a single workshop.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="application-card">
          <span class="persona-tag">Marketing Directors</span>
          <h4>"Content doesn't convert"</h4>
          <p>Try the <strong>One Newsletter</strong> approach — unified messaging for clients AND colleagues.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="application-card">
          <span class="persona-tag">Sales Leaders</span>
          <h4>"Pitches don't resonate"</h4>
          <p>Use the <strong>TED Talk framework</strong> — structure your pitch like a story, not a feature list.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="application-card">
          <span class="persona-tag">Product Leaders</span>
          <h4>"Users don't understand our value"</h4>
          <p>Run <strong>Customer Deep Dives</strong> — 5 structured case study conversations reveal everything.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">Get the Full Playbook</h2>
      <div class="download-box">
        <h3>Solved to Sold</h3>
        <p>The complete Storyselling system: 200+ pages of frameworks, exercises, and worked examples.</p>
        <a href="mailto:dave@wordandmouth.com?subject=Storyselling%20Playbook" class="cta-button">Request the Playbook</a>
        <p class="download-note">Free for serious enquiries</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="article-footer">
      <div class="related-links">
        <h4>Explore Related</h4>
        <a href="/story/">Story Tenet →</a>
        <a href="/clarity/">Clarity Tenet →</a>
        <a href="/services/">How We Work →</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .rabbit-hole {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .hero-rabbit {
    padding: 10rem 2rem 4rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .rabbit-tenets {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .tenet {
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.15);
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .hero-rabbit h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .rabbit-tagline {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  .section {
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #222;
  }

  .section-label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .insight-box {
    background: #111;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .insight-box blockquote {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .insight-box p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .methodology-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 600px) {
    .methodology-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .phase-card {
    background: #111;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }

  .phase-card:hover {
    border-left-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .phase-number {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #000;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 28px;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .phase-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .phase-card p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .phase-card ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .phase-card li {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .concept-box {
    background: #111;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .concept-box h3 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .cycle-visual {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .key-quote {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--muted);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    padding-left: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .stack-container p {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .stack-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 600px) {
    .stack-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .stack-item {
    background: #111;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .stack-item h4 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .stack-item p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .example-box {
    background: #0f0f0f;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .example-box h3 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .example-box p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .outcome {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .client-applications {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .application-card {
    background: #111;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }

  .application-card:hover {
    border-left-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .persona-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.15);
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .application-card h4 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .application-card p {
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .download-box {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a1a 0%, #0f0f0f 100%);
    padding: 3rem;
    text-align: center;
    border: 1px solid #333;
  }

  .download-box h3 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .download-box p {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 500px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  .download-note {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .article-footer {
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #222;
  }

  .related-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .related-links h4 {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .related-links a {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: opacity 0.2s;
  }

  .related-links a:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .endorsement-section {
    border-top: none;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .endorsement-box {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.08) 0%, rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.02) 100%);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding: 2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .endorsement-box blockquote {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .endorsement-box cite {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .endorsement-box cite strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
